  },
  {
    num: '03',
    title: 'Taking an education loan for an MBA or a private law college without checking the placement report',
    body: 'A weak-institute MBA commonly places freshers around Rs 3.5-6 LPA, which rarely clears the loan EMI on a 2-3 year horizon. The same caution applies to a high-fee private law college with a thin placement cell.',
  },
  {
    num: '04',
    title: 'Assuming a certificate alone gets you hired in analytics, marketing, or UX',
    body: 'Employers filter on one real, finished project far more than on a certificate name. A dashboard, a campaign with real spend numbers, or a UX case study with actual user research does more than a stack of course completions.',
  },
  {
    num: '05',
    title: 'Ignoring the CLAT-PG or CUET-PG entrance gate until it is too late',
