  },
  {
    q: 'Is UX/UI design a realistic course for arts and humanities BA graduates?',
    a: 'Yes. UX/UI design is one of the more common pivots for non-design graduates, including arts and commerce students, because hiring is portfolio-based rather than degree-based. Bootcamps run 4-6 months and cost Rs 25,000-1.5 lakh. Fresh bootcamp graduates typically start around Rs 3-7 LPA, with entry-level roles at product companies reaching Rs 6-15 LPA once a strong portfolio is in place.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is a journalism or mass communication postgraduate diploma still worth it?',
    a: 'It depends heavily on the institute and the pivot you make afterward. IIMC reports an average placement package of only Rs 3-4 LPA, though the highest reported package has touched Rs 20 LPA. Pure reporting pay stays modest without a deliberate move into digital strategy, brand journalism, or content leadership, so treat the diploma as a strong entry credential, not a guaranteed high-salary outcome by itself.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which course after BA pays the fastest, not just the most?',
    a: 'Digital marketing and data analytics certifications have the shortest runway to real income among the courses on this list, commonly producing a first paying role inside 3-9 months. Postgraduate degrees and law all delay meaningful income by one to several years in exchange for a stronger long-term ceiling once qualified. Neither approach is automatically wrong; the right one depends on how much runway your finances can absorb before you need a paycheck.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need a specific BA subject to qualify for these courses?',
    a: 'No, for most of them. MBA entrance exams, the 3-year LLB, data analytics and digital marketing certifications, and UX/UI bootcamps do not require a specific BA subject. MA Economics and MA Public Policy are more open than they appear, though a background in economics, political science, or a related subject helps at the strongest institutes. Always verify the exact eligibility criteria on the official admission page before assuming you do or do not qualify.',
  },
];

const faqJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqItems.map((item) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: item.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: item.a },
