  <h2 id="stacking">Why stacking beats picking only one course</h2>

  <p>
    The biggest gap in most "best course after BA" advice is that it treats the decision as pick-one.
  </p>

  <p>
    In practice, the graduates who end up with the strongest income ceiling almost always stack a base
    credential with one visible, provable skill on top. That combination is what actually builds a
    <strong>high-value skill portfolio</strong>, and a portfolio compounds your income in a way a single
    line item on a resume never does.
  </p>

